#Compiling ClipGrab

Pre-compiled packages for ClipGrab are available on https://clipgrab.org
But compiling ClipGrab is really easy!

##Prerequisites

You need to install the Qt6 developer libraries in order to compile the program.

On Ubuntu and Debian-based system, you can install the necessary libraries like this:
sudo apt install qt6-base-dev qt6-webengine-dev qt6-tools-dev qt6-tools-dev-tools qt6-l10n-tools qt6-5compat-dev cmake

Other Linux distributions might have slightly different package names. Packages for Windows and macOS can be downloaded here: https://download.qt.io/

In addition, ffmpeg (no developer libs necessary) needs to be installed.

##Compiling
To compile ClipGrab, simply execute the following commands:

cmake -B build
cmake --build build

This will create an executable "clipgrab" in the build directory that you can start via ./build/clipgrab.
